# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, X2C spinors, GNOF (two coupling
# subspaces, see lih_X2C_gnof_debug.inp), DEBUG TRUE + VERBOSE 1: the PNOF
# counterpart of water_X2C_muller_joint_blocks.inp -- validates the
# real-real, imaginary-imaginary and real-imaginary orbital-rotation
# Hessian blocks (Hessian_opt/PnofHessian.h, L1/L2 pair terms included),
# the joint gradient vector and the joint symmetric Hessian over [t; y]
# against finite differences of the gradient and of the energy, at
# generic fractional frontier occupations and at the optimized ones.
# (The same input with C4_SPINOR TRUE instead of X2C takes ~1 minute:
# many integral rotations at the larger 4-component basis.)
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
DEBUG TRUE
VERBOSE 1
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
HESSIAN_FUNCTIONAL TRUE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
